prompt:
{
  "public_instructions": "You translate natural-language access-control requirements into Cedar policies using the supplied schema. Cedar denies by default. An applicable forbid overrides every permit. Guard optional attributes with has before reading them. Preserve the schema's entity, set, and attribute types. Use only the supplied task information. Do not use tools, files, search, additional model calls, or external feedback. Produce a single final answer as a JSON object with exactly one field, policy, whose value is the complete Cedar policy text. Do not include explanations or Markdown fences.
",
  "harness": {
    "instruction_blocks": [
      "Translate the access-control requirements into a complete Cedar policy set. Identify each action, eligible principal, resource type, required condition, prohibition, and exception. Use only entity types, attributes, actions, and representations supported by the schema. Implement the stated permissions and restrictions together.",
      "Before answering, check the policy mentally for both unauthorized permissions and missing required permissions. Keep distinct action rules separate when their conditions differ. Apply exceptions only to the restriction they qualify. Return one final policy set."
    ],
    "input_order": [
      "requirements",
      "schema"
    ],
    "checklist": [
      "Every required action is covered.",
      "Role, ownership, membership, and context conditions follow the requirements.",
      "Prohibitions and exceptions compose correctly.",
      "Optional attribute reads are guarded and Cedar syntax is valid."
    ]
  },
  "requirements": "The system manages the dispatch of carrier shipments and the confirmation of their delivery.

The people involved are planners, drivers, dispatch managers, depot supervisors, and auditors. One person may hold both the planner and the dispatch manager role at the same time.

The resources are shipments and delivery receipts. Every shipment records its planner, its driver of record, its piece count, its gross weight in kilograms, its status, its tracking code, its origin depot, its hazmat class, and the end of its delivery window. Every delivery receipt records its shipment, its recipient, and when it was signed.

Each request carries the current time, whether it comes from the depot network, whether the shipment has been declared expedited, and whether proof of delivery is present.

In this workflow a shipment is first dispatched and then its delivery is confirmed, and the confirmation step can see the shipment's status and its driver of record as recorded by the dispatch step.

A driver or dispatch manager may dispatch a shipment, but the person who planned the shipment may not be the driver of record who dispatches it, keeping planning and dispatch in different hands.

However, the planner may be the dispatching driver of record when the request originates on the origin depot's network.

The planner may likewise dispatch the shipment when its tracking code carries the assigned carrier prefix.

The same driver of record who dispatched a shipment must be the one to confirm its delivery, and a driver or depot supervisor who was not the dispatching driver of record may not confirm the delivery.

However, a driver or depot supervisor other than the dispatching driver of record may confirm the delivery when the confirmation is submitted from a depot network.

A run through the workflow by a driver who dispatches a shipment they did not plan and then confirms its delivery, tripping no prohibition above, must be able to succeed.",
  "schema": "entity Role enum ["Planner", "Driver", "DispatchManager", "DepotSupervisor", "Auditor"];

entity Depot;

entity User {
    roles: Set<Role>,
};

entity Shipment {
    planner: User,
    driverOfRecord: User,
    pieceCount: Long,
    grossWeightKg: decimal,
    status: String,
    trackingCode: String,
    originDepot: Depot,
    hazmatClass: String,
    deliveryWindowEnd: datetime,
};

entity DeliveryReceipt {
    shipment: Shipment,
    recipient: String,
    signedAt: datetime,
};

action dispatchShipment appliesTo {
    principal: [User],
    resource: [Shipment],
    context: {
        currentTime: datetime,
        fromDepotNetwork: Bool,
        requestDepot?: Depot,
        isExpedited: Bool,
        proofOfDeliveryPresent: Bool,
        trackingCodeCarriesAssignedCarrierPrefix: Bool,
    },
};

action confirmDelivery appliesTo {
    principal: [User],
    resource: [DeliveryReceipt],
    context: {
        currentTime: datetime,
        fromDepotNetwork: Bool,
        requestDepot?: Depot,
        isExpedited: Bool,
        proofOfDeliveryPresent: Bool,
    },
};
"
}
